(7072778, 1074716, 123833, '<td valign="top">Before I joined DPC I came across your amazing photography. The only DPCer I knew about before I knew about DPC. I always thought it involves magic! ;) I still do! Congrats on the well deserved win!</td>', 'Before I joined DPC I came across your amazing photography. The only DPCer I knew about before I knew about DPC. I always thought it involves magic! ;) I still do! Congrats on the well deserved win!', '2013-07-17 10:02:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(7073013, 1074821, 65319, '<td valign="top">LOL...I love an image that has it''s own movie trailer...<a href="//www.youtube.com/watch?v=F-L5bzwdpVI" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Turbo</a>!</td>', 'LOL...I love an image that has it''s own movie trailer...Turbo!', '2013-07-17 18:27:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(7074481, 1074716, 87278, '<td valign="top">Congrats! But whats new?<br/> <br/>The moment I saw in my inbox the name of the contest as Water Drop I was almost sure you wd be winning it. You have so much monopolized anything to do with water drop photography!<br/> <br/>To make for a level playing field, the DPC admins shd make you ''ineligible'' for any contest involving water drops! :)))</td>', 'Congrats! But whats new? The moment I saw in my inbox the name of the contest as Water Drop I was almost sure you wd be winning it. You have so much monopolized anything to do with water drop photography! To make for a level playing field, the DPC admins shd make you ''ineligible'' for any contest involving water drops! :)))', '2013-07-20 09:37:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(7076581, 1074816, 100393, '<td valign="top">Ordinarily I''m not a big fan of water drops. Some folks are so good at them that there ability to offer the wow factor has been diminished - like Hollywood special effects.<br/> <br/>I like what you''ve done here so, the colours are particularly strong and the drop has a floating quality that I like. Couple that with the great combonation of smoothness and sharpness and you have something that is more than the some of its parts.<br/> <br/>I think that is the mark of a good photograph.</td>', 'Ordinarily I''m not a big fan of water drops. Some folks are so good at them that there ability to offer the wow factor has been diminished - like Hollywood special effects. I like what you''ve done here so, the colours are particularly strong and the drop has a floating quality that I like. Couple that with the great combonation of smoothness and sharpness and you have something that is more than the some of its parts. I think that is the mark of a good photograph.', '2013-07-24 16:43:04.000000', NULL, 0),
